<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Discordian Oracle AppleKation ~ reliquary handle

''The old oracle, kept whole — bytes in the CAS, names here.'' The E-Jing-A-Ling Thing throws
sixty-four hexagrams plus `000pi` — the reading a stick or coin gives when it lands on its edge.
The living web AppleKation rides self-contained in one page; beneath it, recovered from the
Wayback strata, the original ''DOA.exe'' of the NeuroAtomic Order of the Nevermind Cabal
(~2001–2003) and the Pentatorah-Zerostore page. The 23 Apples of Eris cabal threw this oracle
daily; the library holds it under its own license: ''Kopyleft — (K) Copyright Is Reversed.
Reprint.'' All Rites Reversed.

Per the content-resolution law, ''the bytes leave the bag'': each artifact rides the `genesis/cas`
KIND-plane at `cid/<sha256>`, and this handle carries name → cid. A session throws the oracle by
opening the DOA.html blob in any browser, offline, forever.

<<~/ahu>>

